From: haskell.nix maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Bound interpreter cleanup and propagate child process failures

Do not rely on pipe EOF to observe child exit: descendants may retain the
pipe writer. Keep GHC pipe descriptors out of the POSIX interpreter, coordinate
Shutdown with the exit watcher, and bound TERM/KILL cleanup of the owned
process group. Poll waitpid so the non-threaded RTS also makes progress.

